<section class="about-what-is">
    <div class="about-what-is-inner">
        <div class="about-what-is-intro">
            <div class="about-what-is-main">
                <h2 class="about-what-is-title">What is the Learning Hub?</h2>
                <p class="about-what-is-lead">
                    The <span class="about-what-is-highlight">make-a-thek Learning Hub</span> is a shared space for learning, discovery and knowledge exchange. It brings together practical learning materials, tools, methodologies, resources and experiences contributed and developed by <span class="about-what-is-highlight">Fab Lab Barcelona, the make-a-thek project and the wider Distributed Design network.</span>
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-what-is-aside">
                <p class="about-what-is-text">
                    Building on the knowledge, resources and experiences accumulated over the years through these initiatives and communities, the Learning Hub connects contributions from diverse fields and practices, including:
                </p>
                <ul class="about-what-is-profiles">
                    {% for profile in ["Makers", "Designers", "Crafters", "Educators", "Researchers", "Practitioners"] %}
                        <li class="about-what-is-profile">{{ profile }}</li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-what-is-journeys">
            <p class="about-what-is-journeys-title">
                By making this collective knowledge accessible in one place, it supports different learning journeys:
            </p>
            <ul class="about-what-is-journeys-list">
                <li>Discover new topics, practices and approaches.</li>
                <li>Experiment with materials and technologies.</li>
                <li>Develop practical skills.</li>
                <li>Share expertise and knowledge.</li>
                <li>Connect with a community of practice.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
